{"name":"Roasted Pistachio","hex":"#c9b27c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roasted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cooked by roasting."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of roast"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roasted"},{"term":"pistachio","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deciduous tree (Pistacia vera) grown in parts of Asia for its drupaceous fruit.","The nutlike fruit of this tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pistachio"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roasting","blocks":[{"text":"Roasting is a cooking method that uses dry heat where hot air covers the food, cooking it evenly on all sides with temperatures of at least 150 °C (300 °F) from an open flame, oven, or other heat source. Roasting can enhance the flavor through caramelization and Maillard browning on the surface of the food. Roasting uses indirect, diffused heat, and is suitable for slower cooking of meat in a larger, whole piece. Meats and most root and bulb vegetables can be roasted. Any piece of meat, especially red meat, that has been cooked in this fashion is called a roast. Meats and vegetables prepared in this way are described as \"roasted\", e.g., roasted chicken or roasted squash."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Roast_Pig_1.JPG/330px-Roast_Pig_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roasting"},{"title":"Pistachio","blocks":[{"text":"The pistachio is a small to medium-sized tree of the cashew family. The tree produces seeds that are widely consumed as food. Pistachios can be used as an ingredient in desserts, chocolate, candy, ice cream, and as a paste or butter. As a tree nut, pistachios are considered a priority allergen that may induce allergic reactions in susceptible people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Pistachio_vera.jpg/330px-Pistachio_vera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pistachio"},{"title":"Shades of chartreuse","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of chartreuse are listed below. Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green, so named because of its resemblance to the color of the French liqueur green chartreuse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg/330px-Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_chartreuse"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG/500px-Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG/1280px-Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG/500px-Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tudor style roasting meat on a spit","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Sunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg/500px-Sunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Sunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg/500px-Sunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Sunday roast consisting of roast beef, potatoes, vegetables, and Yorkshire pudding","link":"https://en.